a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\nmacOS Sequoia 15.1.1 (24B91)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThere's a gap on top of the screen when WINDOW_MODE_MAXIMIZED and Borderless setting is enabled,the gap looks just like a missing title bar size but I think it shouldn't be there with Borderless mode enabled. If you enable \"Extend to Title\" Setting instead of Borderless it fills whole screen but adds button\n\nBorderless\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4b36183b-08b9-48e3-969e-e558040e0e35)\n\nBorderless with dock hiding disabled\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e96f993a-7dde-450a-819d-812ed24df100)\n\nBorderless disabled\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e6065e31-d0db-409e-a97a-05ce47faafc4)\n\nExtend to Title\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/695c253e-c39c-4ff2-ba21-809d34c69456)\n\nExtend to Title with dock hiding disabled\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/01b7ed34-87f2-45f8-91b5-df61a9dfd958)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create new project\n- In project settings change Window Mode to Maximized and enabled Borderless more\n- Add new scene2d\n- add script to root node to visualize window\n```\nextends Node2D\n\nfunc _draw():\n\tdraw_rect(get_viewport_rect(), Color.DARK_BLUE, true)\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[Test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20510819/Test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.gi